175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1- Smooth muscles of GIT \(except in esophagus and proximal part of stomach\) are distinguished by the presence of slow waves known as basic electrical rhythm \(BER\), due to spontaneous rhythmic depolarization and repolarization of membrane potential from -65mv to -45mv.)/Pg 6 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(2- This BER is initiated by pacemaker cells known as interstitial cells of Cajal \(ICCs\). These are stellate mesenchymal cells connected to intestinal smooth muscle fibers by long branched processes. ICCs are located in outer circular muscle layer adjacent to myenteric plexus in stomach and small intestine and show gradual decline in pacemaker frequency. In the colon: they are located at the submucosal border of the circular muscle layer.)/Pg 6 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(3- ICCs give rise to an electrical activity that exhibits sudden and periodical appearance of an upstroke from a resting potential of -70mv.)/Pg 6 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(4- The appearance of the upstroke generates the slow waves in smooth muscle fibers connected with ICCs.)/Pg 6 0 R/K[25]>>
