endobj

538 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(4- pH: 7)/Pg 17 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

539 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(5- Components: Each salivary gland is formed of acini, which secrete a primary secretion that flows through the salivary ducts, which open into the oral cavity)/Pg 17 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

540 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(6- Types:)/Pg 17 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

541 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1381 0 R/E(The parotid glands form about 25% of saliva. )/Pg 17 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

542 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1382 0 R/E(The sublingual glands form about 5% of saliva.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

543 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1383 0 R/E(The submandibular glands acini form about 70% of salivary secretion.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

544 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1384 0 R/E(The buccal glands secrete only mucous.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

545 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 95 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

546 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(7- Mechanism: Salivary secretion consists of two stages;)/Pg 17 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

547 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1385 0 R/E(The first stage: the acini secrete a primary secretion that contains ptyalin and/or mucin in a solution of ions which shows no great difference from extracellular fluid.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

548 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1386 0 R/E(The second stage: As the primary secretion flows through the ducts, the ionic composition of the saliva is markedly modified by the following processes:)/Pg 17 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

549 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1387 0 R/E(Sodium ions \(Na+\) are actively reabsorbed, potassium ions \(K+\) are actively secreted.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

550 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1388 0 R/E(However, sodium reabsorption is higher than potassium secretion in the salivary ducts which causes chloride ions \(CI\) to be passively reabsorbed.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

551 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1389 0 R/E(Therefore, Na+ and Cl concentrations of the saliva are markedly reduced whereas K+ concentration becomes increased during passage through the ducts )/Pg 17 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

552 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(12)/Pg 17 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

553 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 96 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/K[27]>>
endobj

