endobj

561 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1390 0 R/E(Aldosterone increases the K+ concentration and reduces the Na concentration of saliva in an action similar to its action on the kidney.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

562 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1391 0 R/E(Bicarbonate ions \(HCO3\) are actively secreted into the lumen of the duct.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

563 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1392 0 R/E(The ducts are relatively impermeable to water. Therefore, the saliva that reaches the mouth is hypotonic to plasma.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

564 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 96 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

565 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 96 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

566 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1393 0 R/E(The net result of these transport processes under resting conditions makes the concentration of Na+ and Cl in saliva much less, whereas the concentrations of K and HCO3, much more than in plasma.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

567 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E<FEFF2B060020004B002C002000480043004F0033>/Pg 18 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

568 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E<FEFF2B070020004E0061002C00200043006C>/Pg 18 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

569 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1394 0 R/E(During maximal salivation as a result of parasympathetic stimulation, the concentrations of Na, CI and HCO3 in saliva become nearly as in the plasma, and the concentration of K not increased, because ductal modification of the saliva is markedly reduced by the rapid flow in a short time.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[11 12]>>
endobj

