endobj

591 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1404 0 R/E(The buffers in saliva help to keep the oral pH at about 7.0. At this pH, the saliva is saturated with calcium and so the teeth do not lose calcium because Ca dissolves in acidic medium and precipitate in alkaline medium. Loss of Ca from the teeth enamel leads to dental caries.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

592 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1405 0 R/E(Fluoride protects the teeth enamel. It is added in minute amounts to drinking water to be excreted in saliva.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

593 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1406 0 R/E(Proline-rich proteins protect teeth enamel and bind toxic tannins.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

594 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(In the absence of salivation \(xerostomia\), the dry oral-mucosa becomes ulcerated and infected, with a higher incidence of dental caries)/Pg 19 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

