endobj

597 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Saliva contains the digestive enzyme ptyalin \(salivary a-amylase\) that digests starch. This amylase acts in the mouth, and then it is inactivated by the low pH of the stomach, and is reactivated by the high pH of the small intestine)/Pg 19 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

598 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(D- LUBRICATION AND WETTING:)/E(D- LUBRICATION AND WETTING:)/Pg 19 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

599 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1407 0 R/E(Swallowing: Saliva contains mucins \(glycoproteins\) that lubricates the food, facilitating its swallowing,)/Pg 19 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

600 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1408 0 R/E(Speech: Keeping mouth moist facilitates movements of the lips and tongue during speech)/Pg 19 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

601 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1409 0 R/E(Taste: Saliva acts as a solvent for molecules that stimulate taste receptors.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[14]>>
