1000 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1554 0 R/E(Storage of Bile: The bile secreted by the liver cells is normally stored in the gallbladder until needed in the duodenum.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1001 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1555 0 R/E(Concentration of Bile: The maximum volume of the gallbladder is about 20-60 ml, but it can store about 500 ml bile \(24 hours' secretion\). It achieves this through the concentration of hepatic bile. Concentration of bile is caused by removal of sodium by the gallbladder mucosa through an active transport mechanism, which passively draws chloride, bicarbonate and water. The concentrations of bile salts, cholesterol, lecithin and bilirubin are markedly increased.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1002 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1556 0 R/E(Prevention of marked rise in the Intrabiliary pressure: When the Intrabiliary pressure rises, bile secretion will stop.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1003 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1557 0 R/E(Acidification of Bile: This is due to absorption of bicarbonate. Liver bile contains 28 mEq/L HCO3, whereas gallbladder bile contains 10 mEq/L. Acidification of bile keeps lecithin, cholesterol and bile salts in solution inside the gall bladder.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1004 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(CONTROL OF EMPTYING OF THE GALLBLADDER )/Pg 33 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1005 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(= CHOLAGOGUES:)/Pg 33 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

1006 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1558 0 R/E(During digestion, gallbladder contracts, emptying its contents into duodenum.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

1007 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1559 0 R/E(Cholagogues are substances that cause contraction of gallbladder.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

1008 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1\) Cholecytokinin \(CCK\):)/Pg 33 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

1009 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1560 0 R/E(It is the major stimulus for gallbladder contraction and sphincter of Oddi relaxation. Fatty acids and amino acids in the duodenum directly stimulate the secretion of CCK.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

1010 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(2\) Vagal stimulation:)/Pg 33 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

1011 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1561 0 R/E(Vagal stimulation of the gallbladder causes a less strong gallbladder contraction and sphincter of Oddi relaxation.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

1012 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(GALLSTONES: CHOLELITHIASES)/Pg 33 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

1013 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1562 0 R/E(In the USA and Europe, about 85% of gallstones are composed of cholesterol, the remainder are calcium bilirubinate stones.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

1014 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(EFFECT OF CHOLECYSTECTOMY:)/Pg 33 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

1015 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1563 0 R/E(Bile, not the gallbladder; is essential to digestion. After surgical removal of the gallbladder; bile empties slowly but continuously into the intestine, allowing digestion of fats sufficiently to maintain good nutrition and health.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

1016 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1564 0 R/E(However, high-fat meals need to be avoided.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[25]>>
