endobj

1034 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1567 0 R/E(Brunner's glands in the duodenum, which secrete mucus in response to:)/Pg 34 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

1035 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1568 0 R/E(Chemical and physical irritation of the overlying mucosa.)/Pg 34 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

1036 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1569 0 R/E(Cholinergic stimulation: Brunner's glands are inhibited by sympathetic stimulation, thus inhibiting the secretion of protective mucus in the duodenal bulb and this may be one of the factors that cause this area to be the site of peptic ulcers in about 50% of all cases.)/Pg 34 0 R/K[19 20]>>
endobj

1037 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1570 0 R/E(Gastrointestinal hormones, especially secretin.)/Pg 34 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

1038 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(2- Secretion of the Intestinal Alkaline fluid:)/Pg 34 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1039 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1571 0 R/E(The intestinal secretions are formed by the epithelial cells in the crypts of Lieberk\374hn, located on the entire surface of the small intestine in-between the villi.)/Pg 34 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

1040 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1572 0 R/E(Secretions are composed of isotonic fluid of sodium chloride and bicarbonate, formed at a rate of 1800 ml/day, a slightly alkaline pH \(7.5-8.0\).)/Pg 34 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

1041 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1573 0 R/E(The secretions are rapidly absorbed by the villi. This circulation of fluid from the crypts to the villi supplies a watery vehicle for absorption of substances from the chyme as it comes in contact with the villi.)/Pg 34 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

1042 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(3- Enzymes in the Small Intestinal Secretion:)/Pg 34 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

1043 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1574 0 R/E(These enzymes are not secreted into the intestine, but the brush border of the epithelial cells of the mucosa covering the villi contain digestive enzymes that digest some food substances while they are being absorbed. These enzymes are: Peptidases, disaccharidases and intestinal lipase)/Pg 34 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

